{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794172743,"nonce":"A5PKOWOyOO4sf+XwdsHf22iKm90=","title":"gbtracker: multi-repo git-bug manager","message":"## Goal\nOne desktop app that manages every repo using git-bug: add project dirs or parent dirs to scan, discover git-bug repos, browse and filter all epics/tasks/bugs across them, act on them, and run roadmap-open / roadmap-done natively.\n\n## Context\n- `src/mock.rs` — static sample data the UI renders today; replaced by real data.\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:13` — `view()`, the mock screen (top bar, sidebar, Epics page).\n- `src/main.rs:48` — `App` holds only `mode` and `section`.\n- `docs/design.md` — theme rules; all new UI composes `theme::style::*` and `ui::components`, no hardcoded colors.\n- Conventions from the roadmap plugin's `gb` wrapper (`../skillforge/plugins/roadmap/skills/gb/scripts/lib/gb_core.sh:64-74`): `kind:epic|task|bug`, `epic:\u003cfull-id\u003e`, `state:in-progress|blocked`, `L\u003cN\u003e — ` title prefix, done = closed.\n- Planner's call: call the `git-bug` CLI directly from Rust (`-f json`) and port `gb`'s semantics; `gb` lives in a plugin cache path and needs bash + jq.\n- Deps only via `cargo add`, never hand-edit `Cargo.toml`.\n\n## Layers (merge bottom-up)\n1. \u003ckey TBD\u003e — L1 — git-bug read adapter and issue model\n2. \u003ckey TBD\u003e — L2 — Workspace config and git-bug repo discovery\n3. \u003ckey TBD\u003e — L3 — Repositories screen backed by the real workspace\n4. \u003ckey TBD\u003e — L4 — Cross-repo issue list with filters and roadmap-open view\n5. \u003ckey TBD\u003e — L5 — Epics and Overview pages from real data, drop the mock\n6. \u003ckey TBD\u003e — L6 — Issue detail pane\n7. \u003ckey TBD\u003e — L7 — Write actions: close, reopen, state, comment\n8. \u003ckey TBD\u003e — L8 — Roadmap Done: close bugs whose work reached base\n\n## Follow-up (not drafted)\n- Create bug/task/epic from the app (top-bar \"New Bug\", \"New Epic\")\n- Per-repo `git bug push`/`pull` (network) behind the top-bar sync pill\n- Auto-refresh by watching `refs/bugs` (`notify`)\n- Identities, Bridges, Analytics pages\n- Bundle Inter as the default font\n\n## Out of scope\n- Editing titles/bodies, deleting bugs (git-bug has no real delete)\n- Running `/roadmap:impl` from the app\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Every child Task merged\n- Adding `~/personal-space` as a scan folder lists every git-bug repo under it with its issues, filterable, and no mock data remains","files":null}]}